# =============================================================================
# QuickFurno - QF-MVP-80.14C lead-assignment dispatch scheduler.
#
# Deployed to /etc/cron.d/quickfurno-lead-assignment-dispatch (root:root, 0644).
#
# It invokes ONLY the approved root-owned wrapper. There is deliberately no
# curl, no URL, no header and NO SECRET on this line: QF_CRON_SECRET lives only
# in /etc/quickfurno/quickfurno-runtime.env (root-protected) and is read by the
# wrapper at execution time. A cron file is world-readable, so a secret here
# would be a disclosure.
#
# Cadence: once per minute. Overlap is impossible - the wrapper takes an
# exclusive flock and a tick arriving during a slow run exits immediately.
#
# The wrapper sends a fixed batch of 3 (QuickFurno assigns at most 3 vendors per
# lead). Core independently clamps any limit to [1,25].
# =============================================================================
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=""

* * * * * root /usr/local/sbin/qf-lead-assignment-dispatch
